// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// b2-unit-61-philosophy-ethics — "Right and Wrong"
// Vocabulary-domain unit: moral-reasoning and epistemology vocabulary.
//
// Overlap check performed before writing (per this unit's brief):
// - b2-unit-34-abstract-ideas already teaches general philosophy/civic nouns
//   (coscienza, identità, valore, libertà, giustizia, uguaglianza, società,
//   benessere, felicità, significato/senso, verità, etica) paired with
//   correlative grammar. None of those exact words are re-taught here as new
//   tier-1 cards; "la morale" (noun) and "morale" (adjective) are new senses
//   not covered there, and "verità" is only reinforced in passing (never a
//   new tier-1 card in this file).
// - b2-unit-59-advanced-abstract-concepts already teaches il dubbio,
//   l'incertezza, consapevolezza, and the identity/subjectivity cluster. This
//   unit does not re-teach "il dubbio" as a noun — it introduces the verb
//   "dubitare" instead (a genuine word-family extension, not a duplicate),
//   and introduces "la certezza" (the noun u59 only referenced inside a hint
//   for "incertezza," never taught as its own card).
// - b2-unit-40-law-society already teaches "il diritto" and "il dovere" as
//   legal-system nouns. Neither is re-taught here. "colpevole" appears once
//   in that unit's tier-4 passage describing a defendant, but is never its
//   own vocabulary card there — it is taught here for the first time, in the
//   moral (not legal-procedural) sense.
// No new grammar concept: tier 2 reinforces congiuntivo (opinion/doubt/
// impersonal triggers, including the certainty-flips-the-mood contrast),
// relative pronouns (ciò che/quello che/il che/cui), concessive clauses
// (anche se/sebbene/nonostante/benché), si-impersonale/si-passivante,
// infinito sostantivato, correlatives (più...più/sia...che/né...né/o...o),
// and periodo ipotetico (tipo 2 and tipo 3) — all already taught in the
// B1/B2 prerequisite chain — applied to this unit's new ethics/epistemology
// vocabulary in fresh context.
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

